({#˚SIH, ˚SIrByAm#} <ab>&c.</ab>) [{#ASAs-kvip, ata itvam#}]
.²1 A blessing, benediction. (It is thus defined:-- {#vAtsalyAdyatra mAnyena#}
 {#kanizWasyABiDIyate . izwAvaDArakaM vAkyamASIH sA parikIrtitA#}.) {#ASis#}
 is sometimes distinguished from {#vara#}, the former being taken to be
 merely an expression of oneʼs good wishes which may or may not be realized;
 while a {#vara#} is a boon which is more permanent in character and surer
 of fulfilment; <ab>cf.</ab> {#varaH Kalveza nASIH#} <ls>Ś. 4</ls>; {#ASizo gurujanavitIrRA#}
 {#varatAmApadyante#} <ls>K. 291</ls>; {#amoGAH pratigfhRantAvarDyAnupadamASizaH#}
 <ls>R. 1. 44</ls>, <ls n="R.">11. 6</ls>; <ls>Ku. 5. 76</ls>, <ls n="Ku.">7. 47</ls>.
.²2 Act of bestowing a blessing upon others.
.²3 A prayer, wish, desire; {#jagacCaraRyasya nirASizaH sataH#} <ls>Ku. 5. 76</ls>,
 <ls>Bg. 4. 21</ls>, <ls n="Bg.">6. 10</ls>.

.²4 A serpentʼs fang (<ab>cf.</ab> {#ASI#}).
.²5 One of the eight chief medicaments ({#vfdDi#}).

({#ASIrvAdaH#} <ab>&c.</ab>) a blessing, benediction,
 expression of a prayer or wish; {#ASIrvacanasaMyuktAM nityaM yasmAt prakurvate#}
 <ls>S. D. 6</ls>; <ls>Ms. 2. 33</ls>.
